  "body": "## Finding description and impact\nThe Merkl protocol provides `overrideCampaign()` method to allow campaign owners to override an existing campaign. An owner/operator can override campaign as many number of times. There are some safety checks in place to avoid invalid configuration. But the below highlighted check will restrict the owner to update their configuration in some cases. Which should've been a valid operation.\n\nLet's say a protocol wanted to start a campaign in 2 days. The campaign will be 1 month long. But then they postpone it by a month. After a month, if the campaign owner wants to update `duration`, `startTimestamp` or `campaignData` they just can't because as per `newCampaign.duration + _campaign.startTimestamp` check the ••startTimestamp•• considered is the initial timestamp. So, as per this check the campaign is already ended. So, even if this campaign is starting in a few days, as per the below logic `overrideCampaign()` is not allowed. Even though Merkl don't intend to put such restrictions here.\n\n```solidity\n    function overrideCampaign(bytes32 _campaignId, CampaignParameters memory newCampaign) external {\n        CampaignParameters memory _campaign = campaign(_campaignId);\n        _isValidOperator(_campaign.creator);\n        if (\n            newCampaign.rewardToken != _campaign.rewardToken ||\n            newCampaign.amount != _campaign.amount ||\n            (newCampaign.startTimestamp != _campaign.startTimestamp && block.timestamp > _campaign.startTimestamp) || // Allow to update startTimestamp before campaign start\n            // End timestamp should be in the future\n@>          newCampaign.duration + _campaign.startTimestamp <= block.timestamp\n        ) revert Errors.InvalidOverride();\n\n        newCampaign.campaignId = _campaignId;\n        // The manager address cannot be changed\n        newCampaign.creator = _campaign.creator;\n        campaignOverrides[_campaignId] = newCampaign;\n        campaignOverridesTimestamp[_campaignId].push(block.timestamp);\n        emit CampaignOverride(_campaignId, newCampaign);\n    }\n```\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nThe Merkl protocol should consider the new timestamp if the **campaignOverrides** exists for any campaign.\n```diff\n    function overrideCampaign(bytes32 _campaignId, CampaignParameters memory newCampaign) external {\n        CampaignParameters memory _campaign = campaign(_campaignId);\n        _isValidOperator(_campaign.creator);\n++      uint32 startTimestamp = campaignOverrides[_campaignId].campaignId == _campaignId ? campaignOverrides[_campaignId].startTimestamp : _campaign.startTimestamp;\n        if (\n            newCampaign.rewardToken != _campaign.rewardToken ||\n            newCampaign.amount != _campaign.amount ||\n--          (newCampaign.startTimestamp != _campaign.startTimestamp && block.timestamp > _campaign.startTimestamp) || // Allow to update startTimestamp before campaign start\n            // End timestamp should be in the future\n--          newCampaign.duration + _campaign.startTimestamp <= block.timestamp\n++          (newCampaign.startTimestamp != _campaign.startTimestamp && block.timestamp > startTimestamp) || // Allow to update startTimestamp before campaign start\n++          newCampaign.duration + startTimestamp <= block.timestamp\n        ) revert Errors.InvalidOverride();\n\n        newCampaign.campaignId = _campaignId;\n        // The manager address cannot be changed\n        newCampaign.creator = _campaign.creator;\n        campaignOverrides[_campaignId] = newCampaign;\n        campaignOverridesTimestamp[_campaignId].push(block.timestamp);\n        emit CampaignOverride(_campaignId, newCampaign);\n    }\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "In the below PoC following steps occured:\n- Alice created a campaign that is starting in sometime. It's 1 month long\n- Alice postpone the campaign for 35 days.\n- Now, after 30 days Alice wants to update `campaignData` but she can't because as per original campaign config, the campaign has ended already.\n- Even though Alice's campaign has not started yet, still she can't update the config anymore.\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\n\npragma solidity ^0.8.17;\n\nimport { Fixture } from \"../Fixture.t.sol\";\nimport { DistributionCreator, DistributionParameters, CampaignParameters } from \"../../contracts/DistributionCreator.sol\";\nimport { Errors } from \"../../contracts/utils/Errors.sol\";\n\ncontract C4PoC is Fixture {\n    uint256 internal constant maxDistribForOOG = 1e4;\n    uint256 internal constant nbrDistrib = 10;\n    uint32 internal initStartTime;\n    uint32 internal initEndTime;\n    uint32 internal startTime;\n    uint32 internal endTime;\n    uint32 internal numEpoch;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n\n        initStartTime = uint32(block.timestamp);\n        numEpoch = 25;\n        initEndTime = startTime + numEpoch * EPOCH_DURATION;\n\n        vm.prank(governor);\n        creator.setFeeRecipient(dylan);\n\n        vm.startPrank(guardian);\n        address[] memory tokens = new address[](1);\n        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n        tokens[0] = address(angle);\n        amounts[0] = 1e8;\n        creator.setRewardTokenMinAmounts(tokens, amounts);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        angle.mint(address(alice), 1e22);\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        angle.approve(address(creator), type(uint256).max);\n\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        uint256 amount = 100 ether;\n        uint256 amountAfterFees = 90 ether;\n        uint32 startTimestamp = uint32(block.timestamp + 2);\n\n        bytes memory campaignData = abi.encode(\n            0xbEEfa1aBfEbE621DF50ceaEF9f54FdB73648c92C,\n            new address[](0),\n            new address[](0),\n            \"\",\n            new bytes[](0),\n            new bytes[](0),\n            hex\"\"\n        );\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        bytes32 campaignId = creator.createCampaign(\n            CampaignParameters({\n                campaignId: bytes32(0),\n                creator: alice,\n                rewardToken: address(angle),\n                amount: amount,\n                campaignType: 1,\n                startTimestamp: startTimestamp,\n                duration: 3600 * 24 * 30,\n                campaignData: campaignData\n            })\n        );\n\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 1);\n        vm.roll(4);\n\n        // Silo distrib data\n        address[] memory whitelist = new address[](1);\n        whitelist[0] = 0x8095806d8753C0443C118D1C5e5eEC472e30BFeC;\n        bytes memory overrideCampaignData = abi.encode(\n            0x04C0599Ae5A44757c0af6F9eC3b93da8976c150A,\n            2,\n            0xa42001D6d2237d2c74108FE360403C4b796B7170,\n            whitelist,\n            new address[](0),\n            hex\"\"\n        );\n\n        uint32 newStartTimestamp = uint32(block.timestamp + (3600*24*35));\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        creator.overrideCampaign(\n            campaignId,\n            CampaignParameters({\n                campaignId: campaignId,\n                creator: alice,\n                rewardToken: address(angle),\n                amount: amountAfterFees,\n                campaignType: 5,\n                startTimestamp: newStartTimestamp,\n                duration: 3600 * 24 * 30,\n                campaignData: overrideCampaignData\n            })\n        );\n\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + (3600 * 24 * 32));\n        vm.roll(4);\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        vm.expectRevert(Errors.InvalidOverride.selector);\n        creator.overrideCampaign(\n            campaignId,\n            CampaignParameters({\n                campaignId: campaignId,\n                creator: alice,\n                rewardToken: address(angle),\n                amount: amountAfterFees,\n                campaignType: 5,\n                startTimestamp: newStartTimestamp,\n                duration: 3600 * 24 * 30,\n                campaignData: overrideCampaignData\n            })\n        );\n    }\n}\n\n```",
